STALE -- DO NOT RUN cgen_memory_generate.
It has drifted from the shipped ware/rtl/cgen_memory_*.v (different clock port
name, scalar FWD instead of the per-(read,write) matrix, no INIT, no UNDEF
collision matrix, no multiclock variant, opposite multi-write priority) and
running it would overwrite them with semantically different modules. No BUILD
rule references it; it is kept for history only.

The shipped ware/rtl/*.v are hand-maintained, and
inou/cgen/cgen_verilog.cpp::gen_mem_wrapper() emits the matching module inline
for shapes ware/rtl does not ship. Keep those two in lockstep.

--- original notes ---
cgen_memory_generate.cpp
Script written for use with MASC LiveHD/Pyrope
Given a number of read ports and write ports, automatically generates
Verilog memory module with forwarding/latency/masking parameters.

Use: ./cgen_memory_generate read 4 write 2
creates a verilog file with 4 read ports/2 write ports
